WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:06.400
The president of the United States said yesterday
in North Carolina that voter.

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:09.590
Jurors should try to vote twice.

00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:14.679
He actually said you should go out there in
North Carolina.

00:00:14.679 --> 00:00:16.059
Mail in a vote.

00:00:16.059 --> 00:00:19.630
And then on Election Day, go and try to vote.

00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:24.720
Now, Donald Trump is suggesting this as a
sort of test of our election system.

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:31.249
Donald Trump has tried to make the public
believe that our voting systems are so terrible,

00:00:31.249 --> 00:00:38.109
so antiquated, so bogus, that people could
easily get away with mailing in a ballot and

00:00:38.109 --> 00:00:40.970
then going and voting, and then your vote
is counted twice.

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:45.570
Now, if the systems are working correctly,
I've explained this to you.

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:51.820
If you have sent in a ballot and then you
go in to vote in person, it will show up.

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:52.870
You've already voted.

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:56.719
We've already received your ballot via absentee.

00:00:56.719 --> 00:01:01.719
If the opposite happens, imagine for a moment
that you send in a ballot via mail.

00:01:01.719 --> 00:01:03.929
But it hasn't been received on Election Day.

00:01:03.929 --> 00:01:07.790
You go in and vote on Election Day and you're
allowed to.

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:11.440
And then the next day, your mail in ballot
is received.

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:15.800
That ballot would not be counted because you've
already been checked off as having voted.

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:20.590
Now, of course, in a country of 331 million.

00:01:20.590 --> 00:01:21.590
Anything can happen.

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:29.140
And anecdotally, there are probably some cases
of double votes getting by people much like

00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:33.400
there are cases of voting machines going wrong.

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:38.110
And you press one person and accidentally,
you know, or because of manipulation, as some

00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:43.000
would say, casts a ballot for the other guy
or gal.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:45.380
It's a country of 331 million people.

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:51.020
But the idea that that's wide spread and the
idea that that's a good way to win an election

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:53.160
is absolutely laughable.

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:56.870
Well, it's also a felony in North Carolina.

00:01:56.870 --> 00:02:02.170
And here is Donald Trump encouraging voters
to commit a crime.

00:02:02.170 --> 00:02:03.170
Take a look at this.

00:02:03.170 --> 00:02:06.380
Well, they'll go out and they'll vote and
they're going to have to go and check their

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:11.810
vote by going to the polls and voting that
way, because if it if it tabulates, then they

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:13.650
won't be able to do that.

00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:16.780
So let them send it in and let them go.

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:18.390
Vote out of their systems.

00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:21.370
As good as they say it is, then obviously
they won't be able to vote.

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:23.760
If it isn't tabulated, they'll be able to
vote.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:25.469
So that's the way it is.

00:02:25.469 --> 00:02:30.930
But send in your ballots sentiments strong,
whether it's solicited or unsolicited.

00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:32.239
The absentees are fine.

00:02:32.239 --> 00:02:37.520
We have to work to get them, you know, something
and you send them in, but you go to vote.

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:39.730
And if they haven't counted it, you could
vote.

00:02:39.730 --> 00:02:41.819
So that's the way I view it.

00:02:41.819 --> 00:02:43.549
So this is a crime.

00:02:43.549 --> 00:02:44.549
This is a crime.

00:02:44.549 --> 00:02:49.489
The law actually says intentionally double
voting is a crime.

00:02:49.489 --> 00:02:55.049
Put aside the fact that it really would not
